Problem:
A grocery distributor ships crates of produce from two warehouses to three stores. Warehouse A has 300 crates and Warehouse B has 250 crates. The North store needs at least 180 crates, the Central store at least 200, and the South store at least 150. Shipping one crate costs $4 from A to North, $6 from A to Central, $9 from A to South, $7 from B to North, $3 from B to Central, and $5 from B to South. How many crates should go from each warehouse to each store to meet every store's needs at the lowest total shipping cost?

